# .worktreeinclude — untracked paths to copy into a new git worktree.
#
# One path per line, relative to the repo root; blank lines and # comments are
# ignored. A fresh worktree starts without anything git does not track, which
# silently changes behaviour for the gitignored files this repo depends on:
# profiles/local.zsh, claude/*.local.list, and any .env a tool expects.
#
# Deliberately empty. Add a path here only when a worktree genuinely needs it,
# and never add a file that carries a secret -- a worktree is as public as the
# directory it is created in.
